This directory must exist in every release.

cPanel's AutoSSL proves domain ownership by writing a token here and fetching
it over HTTP. The document root is a symlink to the current release, so if a
release does not contain this directory the challenge has nowhere to land and
the certificate quietly fails to renew — about ninety days after anyone would
have thought to check.

Anything AutoSSL writes here is wiped by the next deploy, which is fine: the
token is fetched within seconds of being written.
